# Saving and restoring the cursor: DECSC and DECRC (ESC 7, ESC 8) and SCOSC and SCORC (CSI s, CSI u).
#
# VT510 DECSC: the cursor position, the SGR rendition, the character sets in GL and GR, the origin
# mode and the selective erase attribute are saved.

test DECSC and DECRC save and restore the position
spec VT510 DECSC/DECRC; xterm ctlseqs ESC 7, ESC 8
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e7\e[4;5H\e8x
screen
|          |
|  x       |
cursor 2,4

test DECRC restores the rendition
spec VT510 DECSC: the SGR attributes are saved
size 10 4
feed \e[1;31m\e7\e[0m\e8x
cell 1,1 text=x fg=idx:1 attrs=bold

test the rendition set after the save does not come back
spec VT510 DECRC
size 10 4
feed \e7\e[1;31m\e8x
cell 1,1 text=x fg=default attrs=none

test DECRC restores the character set
spec VT510 DECSC: the character sets in GL and GR are saved
size 10 4
feed \e(0\e7\e(B\e8q
screen
|─|

test DECRC restores the origin mode
spec VT510 DECSC: the state of origin mode is saved
known-fail: alacritty – DECRC does not restore the origin mode
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3r\e[?6h\e7\e[?6l\e8\e[1;1Hx
screen
|          |
|x         |

test DECRC restores the selective erase attribute
spec VT510 DECSC: the selective erase attribute is saved
size 10 4
feed \e[1"q\e7\e[0"q\e8A\e[1;1H\e[?2K
screen
|A         |

test DECRC can restore the same state more than once
spec VT510 DECRC
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e7\e[4;5H\e8\e[4;5H\e8x
cursor 2,4

test a second DECSC replaces the first
spec VT510 DECSC: one saved state
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e7\e[3;4H\e7\e[1;1H\e8x
cursor 3,5

test DECRC with nothing saved goes home
convention a terminal starts with the home position saved; DECSTR lists "Save cursor state: home position"
size 10 4
feed \e[3;3H\e8x
screen
|x         |
cursor 1,2

test DECRC with nothing saved resets the rendition
convention a terminal starts with the normal rendition saved
size 10 4
feed \e[1;31m\e8x
cell 1,1 text=x fg=default attrs=none

test SCOSC and SCORC save and restore the position
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI s saves the cursor (SCOSC), CSI u restores it (SCORC)
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3H\e[s\e[4;5H\e[u
cursor 2,3

test SCORC restores the rendition like DECRC
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI u restores the cursor (SCORC, also ANSI.SYS)
size 10 4
feed \e[4m\e[s\e[0m\e[ux
cell 1,1 text=x attrs=underline

test a soft reset forgets the saved cursor
spec VT510 DECSTR: "Save cursor state: home position"
known-fail: alacritty – DECSTR (CSI ! p) is not implemented
size 10 4
feed \e[3;3H\e7\e[!p\e8x
screen
|x         |

test a full reset forgets the saved cursor
spec VT510 RIS: returns the terminal to its initial state
size 10 4
feed \e[3;3H\e7\ec\e8x
screen
|x         |

test DECRC restores the hyperlink
convention OSC 8 calls the hyperlink "a cell attribute like color", and DECSC saves the rendition
size 20 4
feed \e]8;;http://a.example\a\e7\e]8;;\a\e8x
cell 1,1 text=x link=http://a.example

test DECRC brings back the state of no hyperlink
convention the same: a link that was not open when DECSC saved is not open after DECRC
size 20 4
feed \e7\e]8;;http://a.example\a\e8x
cell 1,1 text=x link=none
